IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `sgia-p2-written-law`

-- Tests for sgia-p2-written-law.l4 (ss 3 to 9B, 11 to 18). Expected values are written from the text of each section.

§ `s 3, 4, 5, 6`

#ASSERT `an Act is judicially noticed as a public Act` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`an Act is judicially noticed as a public Act` TRUE)
-- s 4: "if there be more enactments than one": 1 enactment needs no sections, 2 do
#ASSERT NOT (`an Act must be divided into sections` 1)
#ASSERT `an Act must be divided into sections` 2
#ASSERT `an Act must be divided into sections` 30
#ASSERT `a section is a substantive enactment` FALSE
#ASSERT `a section is a substantive enactment` TRUE
#ASSERT `is part of the Act and has effect as part of it` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `is part of the Act and has effect as part of it` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`is part of the Act and has effect as part of it` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the division of an Act is taken notice of in all courts and for all purposes` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the division of an Act is taken notice of in all courts and for all purposes` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the division of an Act is taken notice of in all courts and for all purposes` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 7: forms`

#ASSERT `a deviation from a prescribed form invalidates it` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- each condition failing leaves the Act silent on invalidity
#ASSERT `a deviation from a prescribed form invalidates it` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a deviation from a prescribed form invalidates it` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a deviation from a prescribed form invalidates it` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a deviation from a prescribed form invalidates it` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a deviation from a prescribed form invalidates it` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 7A: examples and illustrations`

#ASSERT `the example or illustration is exhaustive` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the example or illustration is exhaustive` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `which prevails when an example is inconsistent with the provision` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the provision prevails`
#ASSERT `which prevails when an example is inconsistent with the provision` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `which prevails when an example is inconsistent with the provision` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 8: mode of referring to written laws`

#ASSERT `it is sufficient for all purposes to refer to the written law in this way` `the year of its enactment and its number among the Acts enacted in that year` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it is sufficient for all purposes to refer to the written law in this way` `the year of its enactment and its number among the Acts enacted in that year` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `it is sufficient for all purposes to refer to the written law in this way` `its short title` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it is sufficient for all purposes to refer to the written law in this way` `its short title` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `it is sufficient for all purposes to refer to the written law in this way` `its chapter number and the year of the revised edition` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it is sufficient for all purposes to refer to the written law in this way` `its chapter number and the year of the revised edition` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `it is sufficient for all purposes to refer to the written law in this way` `the citation the subsidiary legislation provides for` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it is sufficient for all purposes to refer to the written law in this way` `the citation the subsidiary legislation provides for` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `it is sufficient for all purposes to refer to the written law in this way` `the citation the subsidiary legislation provides for` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a reference may be made according to a copy of a written law` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a reference may be made according to a copy of a written law` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the reference is read as a reference to the written law as amended from time to time` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the reference is read as a reference to the written law as amended from time to time` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the reference is read as a reference to the written law as amended from time to time` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the reference is read as a reference to the changed short title or citation` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the reference is read as a reference to the changed short title or citation` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the reference is read as a reference to the changed short title or citation` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the reference is read as a reference to the changed short title or citation` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 9, 9A, 9B`

#ASSERT `where a reference by number or letter only points` `a section, Part, Chapter or Schedule` TRUE EQUALS JUST `the Act in which the reference occurs`
#ASSERT `where a reference by number or letter only points` `a subsection, paragraph or sub-paragraph` TRUE EQUALS JUST `the section in which the reference occurs`
#ASSERT `where a reference by number or letter only points` `a section, Part, Chapter or Schedule` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 9 applies, with suitable modification` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`section 9 applies, with suitable modification` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the interpretation to be preferred` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the first interpretation`
#ASSERT `the interpretation to be preferred` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the second interpretation`
#ASSERT `the interpretation to be preferred` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the interpretation to be preferred` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to the material` TRUE `to confirm the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text, in its context and with its purpose` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to the material` TRUE `to ascertain the meaning when the provision is ambiguous or obscure` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to the material` TRUE `to ascertain the meaning when the ordinary meaning leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or unreasonable` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to the material` FALSE `to ascertain the meaning when the provision is ambiguous or obscure` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 9A(3) names the material as material that may be considered` `an explanatory statement relating to the Bill` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 9A(3) names the material as material that may be considered` `the Minister's second reading speech` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 9A(3) names the material as material that may be considered` `relevant material in an official record of debates in Parliament` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 9A(3) names the material as material that may be considered` `a treaty or other international agreement referred to in the written law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 9A(3) names the material as material that may be considered` `a document declared by the written law to be a relevant document` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 9A(3) names the material as material that may be considered` `matters in the document containing the text of the written law, as printed or published by the Government Printer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 9A(3) names the material as material that may be considered` `any other material` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT count `the matters to which regard must be had in deciding whether to consider material and what weight to give it` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the ideas are taken to be different merely because the forms of words differ` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the ideas are taken to be different merely because the forms of words differ` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the ideas are taken to be different merely because the forms of words differ` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 11 to 14: repeal and its consequences`

-- s 11: remains in force so far as not inconsistent and until revoked or replaced, unless a contrary intention appears
#ASSERT `the subsidiary legislation remains in force after the Act or part is repealed` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the subsidiary legislation remains in force after the Act or part is repealed` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the subsidiary legislation remains in force after the Act or part is repealed` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the subsidiary legislation remains in force after the Act or part is repealed` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the subsidiary legislation remains in force after the Act or part is repealed` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the last repeal revives the written law or provisions previously repealed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the last repeal revives the written law or provisions previously repealed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the last repeal revives the written law or provisions previously repealed` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the repeal is deemed to include the repeal of the amending written law` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the repeal is deemed to include the repeal of the amending written law` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal is deemed to include the repeal of the amending written law` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the repealed written law remains in force` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the repealed written law remains in force` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the repealed written law remains in force` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 15`

#ASSERT `the reference includes the other written law as amended from time to time` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the reference includes the other written law as amended from time to time` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the reference includes the other written law as amended from time to time` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a reference to the provision repealed is construed as a reference to the provision re-enacted` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to the provision repealed is construed as a reference to the provision re-enacted` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a reference to the provision repealed is construed as a reference to the provision re-enacted` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `subsidiary legislation made or a thing done under the provision repealed has effect as if made or done under the provision re-enacted` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsidiary legislation made or a thing done under the provision repealed has effect as if made or done under the provision re-enacted` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `subsidiary legislation made or a thing done under the provision repealed has effect as if made or done under the provision re-enacted` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `subsidiary legislation made or a thing done under the provision repealed has effect as if made or done under the provision re-enacted` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 16: effect of repeal`

#ASSERT `the repeal does this` `revive anything not in force or existing when the repeal takes effect` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal does this` `affect the previous operation of the repealed law or anything duly done or suffered under it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal does this` `affect a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal does this` `affect a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred for an offence against it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal does this` `affect an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, liability or penalty` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a contrary intention, or no repeal at all: the Act does not say
#ASSERT `the repeal does this` `affect a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the repeal does this` `affect a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `it may be instituted, continued or enforced, or the penalty imposed, as if the repealing law had not been passed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it may be instituted, continued or enforced, or the penalty imposed, as if the repealing law had not been passed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `it may be instituted, continued or enforced, or the penalty imposed, as if the repealing law had not been passed` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 16 treats the event as a repeal` `a repeal effected by implication` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 16 treats the event as a repeal` `the abrogation or limitation of the effect of the written law or part` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 16 treats the event as a repeal` `the exclusion of the application of the written law or part to any person, subject matter or circumstance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 16 treats the event as a repeal` `the expiry, lapse or other ceasing to have effect of the written law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 16 treats the event as a repeal` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `is a part of a written law for section 16` `a provision` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a part of a written law for section 16` `words` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a part of a written law for section 16` `figures` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a part of a written law for section 16` `drawings` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a part of a written law for section 16` `symbols` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a part of a written law for section 16` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 17, 18`

#ASSERT `the amending Act is construed as one with the amended Act and as part of it` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the amending Act is construed as one with the amended Act and as part of it` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the amending Act is construed as one with the amended Act and as part of it` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the amending Act is construed as one with the amended Act and as part of it` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the proceeding may be continued as if the written law continued in force` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the proceeding may be continued as if the written law continued in force` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the proceeding may be continued as if the written law continued in force` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the proceeding may be continued as if the written law continued in force` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
